  "taskPrune": "Prune",
  "guideCheckSoil": "Push a finger 2–3 cm into the soil, or about a third of the way down the pot. Water only if it feels dry, then water slowly until it drains from the bottom. Early morning is best; water the base, not the leaves.",
  "guideCheckSoilDry": "This plant should dry out between waterings (succulents completely). Check the soil and water only when it is dry; overwatering is the main risk.",
  "guideCheckSoilMoist": "Don't let this plant's soil dry out. Check it and water if it is getting dry.",
  "guideInspectPests": "Look under leaves and on new growth for aphids, mites and whitefly; aphids gather on the upwind side. Wash pests off with a strong jet of water early in the day. Avoid broad-spectrum sprays: they can make mites worse.",
  "guideFeed": "Feed every 2–4 weeks while the plant is growing, onto moist soil, at the amount on the product label. Feed less if plants turn tall and spindly or leaf edges look burnt.",
  "guideTransplant": "Seedlings raised in trays are moved to their final container about 25–30 days after sowing; most vegetables are ready at 2–3 true leaves.",
  "guideHarvest": "By the sourced timeline this crop may be ready to start harvesting. Timing varies with variety and season and is counted from sowing, so plants started as seedlings may be ready sooner.",
